class:: StereoCoherence
summary:: Averaged magnitude-squared coherence within a frequency band
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/FFT

description::
Each Hann-windowed frame updates exponentially averaged left/right power and complex cross power. Each bin contributes |P_LR|.squared/(P_LL*P_RR), averaged across the selected band with shared-energy weights 2*sqrt(P_LL*P_RR). This is an averaged spectral coherence estimator following the cross-spectrum definition used in Welch analysis, with exponential averaging in place of a finite segment average. Four frames are required before output; stationarity over averageTime remains necessary.

Uses two private radix-2 FFTs and precomputed Hann windows. frameSize and hop are fixed at construction. CPU is O(frameSize*log(frameSize)) per hop; all storage is allocated before processing. First output is available after frameSize/sampleRate, with coherence held at zero for another three hops; reliable averaging takes approximately averageTime. Frequency selection is quantized to FFT bins. Source for the cross-spectral definition: link::https://www.mathworks.com/help/signal/ref/mscohere.html::.

Vanilla FFT exposes separate spectral frames; this UGen combines two channels and maintains cross-spectral averages.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: frameSize
Literal FFT power of two, 256..8192.

argument:: hop
Literal frame fraction, 0.0625..1; default 0.5.

argument:: averageTime
Exponential spectral averaging constant, clipped to 0.01..10 seconds.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; zero means Nyquist.

returns::
Coherence from zero through one; silence or no shared energy returns zero.

examples::
StereoCoherence measures the magnitude-squared cross-spectral coherence between two audio channels within a specified frequency band (0 for uncorrelated/diffuse sound, 1 for fully coherent linear relationship). In this example, low coherence (indicating diffuse ambient reverberation or room decorrelation) automatically opens an ambient stereo reverb send, while highly coherent direct sound remains crisp and upfront. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time stereo coherence.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~miraBuffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var coh = StereoCoherence.kr(source[0], source[1], frameSize: 1024, hop: 0.5, averageTime: 0.2, minFreq: 200, maxFreq: 5000);
        var cohLag = coh.lag(0.08);
        var diffuseSend = (1 - cohLag).clip(0, 1) * 0.5;
        var wet = FreeVerb2.ar(source[0], source[1], 1.0, 0.7, 0.3) * diffuseSend;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + wet;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, cohLag.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Stereo Coherence", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0, "index");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
